TITLE:: FSSteiner
summary:: Virtual Analog Model of the Steiner-Parker Multimode Diode VCF
categories:: UGens>Filters
related:: Classes/FSWasp, Classes/MS20Diode, Classes/MS20OTA

DESCRIPTION::
FSSteiner is a virtual analog model of the legendary multimode diode-based filter originally designed by Nyle Steiner in 1974 for the Steiner-Parker Synthacon and SynthaSystem synthesizers.

Unlike ladder filters or state-variable filters that use a single audio input with multiple output taps, the Steiner-Parker filter uses a modified Sallen-Key topology with strong inter-stage loading and distinct physical input injection nodes for Low-Pass (LP), Band-Pass (BP), and High-Pass (HP) modes, feeding into a unified active output.

This model is derived from the original circuit analysis by Nyle Steiner (Electronic Design, 1974) and modern adaptations (Yves Usson YuSynth / Yasunori Hirakawa), featuring a topology-preserving transform (TPT) zero-delay capacitor state space and an anti-parallel diode limiter in the positive feedback loop.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: ar

ARGUMENT:: in
Audio-rate input signal.

ARGUMENT:: freq
Filter cutoff frequency in Hertz (10 Hz to 0.49 * sampleRate). Supports audio rate and control rate.

ARGUMENT:: res
Resonance parameter in [0.0, 1.0], mapping to the feedback gain K (0.0 to 3.6). Self-oscillation begins around res = 0.83 (K = 3.0) and stabilizes into a bounded limit cycle via the diode limiter.

ARGUMENT:: mode
Filter mode selection (integer, init-only):
TABLE::
## 0 || Low-Pass (12 dB/octave)
## 1 || Band-Pass (symmetric 6 dB/octave skirts)
## 2 || High-Pass (12 dB/octave with characteristic +6 dB/octave zero transition)
::

ARGUMENT:: drive
Overdrive factor (default 1.0, range [0.0, 20.0]).
When set to 0.0, runs the pure linear small-signal model.
When set > 0.0, runs the nonlinear model with diode feedback limiting and saturation.

returns:: An audio-rate filtered signal.

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
// Boot server
s.boot;

// 1. Low-Pass sweep with saw oscillator
(
x = {
    var src = Saw.ar([110, 110.5]) * 0.2;
    var cutoff = SinOsc.kr(0.2).exprange(100, 8000);
    FSSteiner.ar(src, freq: cutoff, res: 0.6, mode: 0, drive: 1.0) * 0.3;
}.play;
)
x.free;

// 2. Band-Pass noise sweep with high resonance
(
x = {
    var src = PinkNoise.ar(0.3 ! 2);
    var cutoff = SinOsc.kr(0.15).exprange(200, 4000);
    var res = Line.kr(0.1, 0.95, 4);
    FSSteiner.ar(src, freq: cutoff, res: res, mode: 1, drive: 1.0) * 0.25;
}.play;
)
x.free;

// 3. Autonomous Diode Self-Oscillation Limit Cycle (res = 0.95)
(
x = {
    var trig = Impulse.ar(1) * 0.1;
    var cutoff = SinOsc.kr(0.3).exprange(300, 1500);
    FSSteiner.ar(trig, freq: cutoff, res: 0.95, mode: 0, drive: 1.0) * 0.25;
}.play;
)
x.free;
::
